<title>UK: London's King's Cross station shut for bomb scare.</title>
<headline>London's King's Cross station shut for bomb scare.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>London's King's Cross railway station was shut down on Friday after police received a call that a bomb had been planted there.</p>
<p>A police spokeswoman, speaking by telephone, said bomb disposal squads were searching the station for a possible device. The railway stations at Waterloo and Euston were shut briefly after similar bomb scares but had since reopened.</p>
</text>
